2309:Constants starting with `\e` are
2310-[ANSI escape sequences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ANSI_escape_code).
2311-
2312-`CLEAR` clears the screen, similar to the `clear` command. The rest are of the
2313-form `\e[Nm`, where `N` is an integer, and set terminal display attributes.
2314-
2315-Terminal display attribute escape sequences can be combined, for example text
2316-weight `BOLD`, text style `STRIKETHROUGH`, foreground color `CYAN`, and
2317-background color `BG_BLUE`. They should be followed by `NORMAL`, to reset the
2318-terminal back to normal.
2319-
2320-Escape sequences should be quoted, since `[` is treated as a special character
2321-by some shells.
2322-
2323-```just
2324-@foo:
2325-  echo '{{BOLD + STRIKETHROUGH + CYAN + BG_BLUE}}Hi!{{NORMAL}}'
2326-```
